monthly), and 600 mg (single dose) cohorts of the ongoing <FONT STYLE="white-space:nowrap">RestorAATion-2</FONT> clinical trial that demonstrated <FONT STYLE="white-space:nowrap">WVE-006</FONT> achieved key AATD treatment goals by recapitulating an <FONT
STYLE="white-space:nowrap">MZ-like</FONT> phenotype, including robust, dose-dependent reductions of circulating, mutant <FONT STYLE="white-space:nowrap">Z-AAT</FONT> protein, with corresponding increases in wild-type
<FONT STYLE="white-space:nowrap">M-AAT</FONT> protein, and restoration of dynamic AAT response. Wave expects to share data from the 600 mg (monthly) multidose cohort in the second half of 2026. </P></TD></TR></TABLE>
